Pensions Plans Agreements

This Pensions Plans Agreements (the "Agreements") is made and entered into as of this 2nd day of February, 2018 (the "Successful Date"), by and between PQR Corp., a Wilmington Corp. (the "Co."), and the eligible Attendees (the "Attendees") under the Co.'s Bottom-Hats Plans (the "Plans").

1. Eligibility

An employee of the Co. will be eligible to participate in the Plans if they meet the following criteria:

a. The employee is a member of the Co.'s management team or a highly compensated employee;

b. The employee has attained the age of 19;

c. The employee has completed at least one year of service with the Co.; and

d. The employee is a citizen or legal resident of of States United.

2. Contributions

The Co. will make contributions to the Plans on behalf of each eligible participant. The contribution amount will be determined by the Co.'

based on the participant's compensation and other factors. The Co. will contribute a minimum of 3% of each participant's compensation, up to a maximum of 10%.

3. Investments Options

The assets of the Plans will be held in a trust and invested in a diversified portfolio of investments. The Attendees will have the option to choose from a variety of Investments options, including:

a. Large-cap stocks;

b. Large-cap stocks;

c. Internation stocks;

d. Bonds;

e. Cash market funds; and

f. Target-date funds.

4. Distribution Rules

Distributions from the Plans will be made in accordance with the following rules:

